### STAP 1: Login als Henk en bewaar het kortlevende token (zet om te tseten geldigheid voor 10 seconden)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "Henk",
  "password": "pwd"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("userHenkToken", response.body.token);
    client.log("Token ontvangen: " + response.body.token);
%}

### STAP 2: Direct verzoek uitvoeren (BINNEN 10 seconden) -> Verwacht: 200 OK
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

> {%
    client.test("Token is nog geldig: status 200", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Verwachtte 200 OK maar kreeg " + response.status);
    });
%}

### PAUZE: Wacht nu handmatig 10 tot 15 seconden totdat het token verlopen is...

### STAP 3: Hetzelfde verzoek opnieuw uitvoeren (NA 5 seconden) -> Verwacht: 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

> {%
    client.test("Token is verlopen: status 401 Unauthorized", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 401, "Verwachtte 401 Unauthorized maar kreeg " + response.status);
    });
%}

### STAP 4: Aantonen dat ook andere endpoints nu direct geblokkeerd worden
GET http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/my-incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

> {%
    client.test("Ook incidenten ophalen mislukt: status 401", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 401, "Verwachtte 401 Unauthorized");
    });
%}

### Try change role fails: a normal USER cannot promote themself to OFFICIAL, but an ADMIN can
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/2/role
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

{
  "role": "OFFICIAL"
}

### Report a new incident
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

{
  "category": "ENVIRONMENT",
  "description": "Electricity down in our street",
  "latitude": 51.5907258900,
  "longitude": 4.8148889134,
  "priority": "CRITICAL"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("newIncidentByHenk", response.body.id);
%}

### Update reported incident
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/{{newIncidentByHenk}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

{
  "description": "Update: Electricity down in the whole block!"
}

### Try to change status of own incident fails: this restricted based on the business rules)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/{{newIncidentByHenk}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

{
  "status": "RESOLVED"
}

### Get all my incidents
GET http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/my-incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

### Upload an image to incident 5
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/{{newIncidentByHenk}}/images
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="kapotte brievenbus.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ../testimages/kapotte brievenbus.jpeg
--WebAppBoundary--

### Get all my incidents
GET http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/my-incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}

### Get an image api/incidents/images
GET http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/images/incident5-image1.jpg
Authorization: Bearer {{userHenkToken}}
